.TH MCP-SCAFFOLD 1
.SH NAME
mcp\-scaffold \- Programmable scaffolder + migrator for mcp\-cli\-starter\-template
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmcp\-scaffold\fR [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Programmable scaffolder + migrator for mcp\-cli\-starter\-template
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Log debug\-level info to stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Non\-interactive: accept defaults for any unset value
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-banner\fR
Suppress the ascii banner
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinit\fR
Fresh scaffold into <target> (defaults to cwd)
.TP
\fBapply\fR
Apply migrations to an existing repo
.TP
\fBplan\fR
Dry\-run preview of which migrations would apply
.TP
\fBmigrate\fR
Run a single migration or one whole phase
.TP
\fBadd\-mcp\-app\fR
Add a second MCP app to apps/<name>\-mcp/ inside an existing scaffolded repo
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List discovered phases + migrations
.SH "MCP-SCAFFOLD INIT"
Fresh scaffold into <target> (defaults to cwd)
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR mcp\-scaffold init [OPTIONS] [<target>]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<name>\fR
Tool name (kebab\-case, BARE — no \-mcp suffix)
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fI<scope>\fR
Npm scope, with leading @
.TP
\fB\-\-package\-manager\fR \fI<pm>\fR
pnpm | npm | bun (fresh scaffolds require pnpm; existing repos auto\-detect)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Skip the Ink/React TUI surface
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-http\fR
Skip the Streamable HTTP transport
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-rust\-accel\fR
Skip the optional Rust acceleration crate
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-semantic\-release\fR
Skip the semantic\-release workflow
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<target>\fR
Target directory (defaults to cwd)
.SH "MCP-SCAFFOLD APPLY"
Apply migrations to an existing repo
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR mcp\-scaffold apply [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fI<dir>\fR
Path to the existing repo
.TP
\fB\-\-execute\fR
Actually apply (default is dry\-run)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite files that diverge from the template (default: preserve user customizations)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<name>\fR
Tool name (kebab\-case, BARE — no \-mcp suffix)
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fI<scope>\fR
Npm scope, with leading @
.TP
\fB\-\-package\-manager\fR \fI<pm>\fR
pnpm | npm | bun (fresh scaffolds require pnpm; existing repos auto\-detect)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Skip the Ink/React TUI surface
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-http\fR
Skip the Streamable HTTP transport
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-rust\-accel\fR
Skip the optional Rust acceleration crate
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-semantic\-release\fR
Skip the semantic\-release workflow
.SH "MCP-SCAFFOLD PLAN"
Dry\-run preview of which migrations would apply
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR mcp\-scaffold plan [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fI<dir>\fR
Path to target repo
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI<mode>\fR
\&'new' or 'existing' (default: existing)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<name>\fR
Tool name (kebab\-case, BARE — no \-mcp suffix)
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fI<scope>\fR
Npm scope, with leading @
.TP
\fB\-\-package\-manager\fR \fI<pm>\fR
pnpm | npm | bun (fresh scaffolds require pnpm; existing repos auto\-detect)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Skip the Ink/React TUI surface
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-http\fR
Skip the Streamable HTTP transport
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-rust\-accel\fR
Skip the optional Rust acceleration crate
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-semantic\-release\fR
Skip the semantic\-release workflow
.SH "MCP-SCAFFOLD MIGRATE"
Run a single migration or one whole phase
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR mcp\-scaffold migrate [OPTIONS] <id>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fI<dir>\fR
Path to target repo
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI<mode>\fR
\&'new' or 'existing' (default: existing)
.TP
\fB\-\-execute\fR
Actually apply (default is dry\-run)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite divergent files (default: preserve in existing mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<name>\fR
Tool name (kebab\-case, BARE — no \-mcp suffix)
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fI<scope>\fR
Npm scope, with leading @
.TP
\fB\-\-package\-manager\fR \fI<pm>\fR
pnpm | npm | bun (fresh scaffolds require pnpm; existing repos auto\-detect)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Skip the Ink/React TUI surface
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-http\fR
Skip the Streamable HTTP transport
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-rust\-accel\fR
Skip the optional Rust acceleration crate
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-semantic\-release\fR
Skip the semantic\-release workflow
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<id>\fR
e.g. 04\-robustness/m1\-robustness\-pkg, or just 04\-robustness
.SH "MCP-SCAFFOLD ADD-MCP-APP"
Add a second MCP app to apps/<name>\-mcp/ inside an existing scaffolded repo
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR mcp\-scaffold add\-mcp\-app [OPTIONS] <name>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fI<dir>\fR
Path to the scaffolded repo
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fI<scope>\fR
Npm scope, with leading @. Auto\-detected from existing apps/*\-mcp/ if omitted.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Skip the Ink/React TUI surface for the new app
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-http\fR
Skip the Streamable HTTP transport for the new app
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-rust\-accel\fR
Skip the rust\-accel workspace dep for the new app
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<name>\fR
Bare tool name for the new app (no \-mcp suffix)
